    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec asked that on a successful owner create, a welcome notification be enqueued by emitting a line via the logger named `NOTIFY` containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (which backs the sole `POST /api/owners` endpoint), I:\n\n1. Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. After the owner is persisted and the existing audit lines are emitted, added the welcome-notification line:\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nPlacing it after `saveOwner` ensures the id and the assigned `memberId` are both populated, and only successful creates reach this point (validation/duplicate failures throw earlier).\n\n## Verification\n\n- The new `Cp57Tests` passes \u2014 the captured `NOTIFY` output confirms `NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2616E6609E3`.\n- Full suite: **Tests run: 69, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.",
